RefGuard - Reference Integrity & Citation Quality Checker

Copyright (c) 2026 RefGuard contributors.

RefGuard verifies bibliography metadata against public scholarly sources and
produces evidence-based reports. Reference identity decisions are based on
metadata matching and evidence fusion, not on LLM output.

Optional LLM relevance checks may send citation context and bibliographic
metadata to the provider configured by the user. They are disabled by default.
Do not commit provider API keys or private documents.

Public data sources used by RefGuard may include Crossref, OpenAlex, arXiv,
DBLP, and Semantic Scholar. Users are responsible for complying with each
source's terms of use and rate limits.
